  "subject": "a fifth-grader in Taipei who forges his mother's signature in the school contact book after a bad quiz, practises it thirty times, adds a little heart, and is caught because his mother always signs with a smiley face",
  "caption": "1980s boogie-funk with horn stabs, Mandarin. Slap bass locked with tight drums and handclaps, rhythm guitar with wah on sixteenth-note chops, trumpet and tenor sax stabs answering the vocal, Fender Rhodes chords. Tight dry funk mix, bright horn section, crisp hi-hats. Female vocal, bright mid-register, punchy and clearly sung. 112 BPM, E minor. Cheeky, bouncy comic panic. No rap, no trap hi-hats, no autotune, no EDM drop, no distorted guitar. Clear full voice, every word enunciated, steady sung melody on every line.",
  "lyrics": "[Intro - slap bass, horn stabs, handclaps]\n[Verse 1]\n聯絡簿翻到最後一頁\n老師用紅筆圈了一圈\n家長簽名那一格空白\n我的心跳比下課鐘還快\n[Pre-Chorus]\n媽媽出差到禮拜五\n考卷可不能等到那一天\n[Chorus]\n簽簽簽 練了三十遍\n媽媽的名字我寫得很像\n簽簽簽 手千萬別抖\n最後一撇要拉得漂亮\n[Verse 2]\n隔天老師瞇著眼睛看\n說這個簽名真有氣質\n我還特別加了一顆愛心\n老師說 媽媽上次畫笑臉\n[Pre-Chorus]\n我的腳趾縮在鞋子裡\n全班都轉過頭來看\n[Chorus]\n簽簽簽 練了三十遍\n媽媽的笑臉我忘記畫\n簽簽簽 手還是在抖\n最後一撇再漂亮也沒用\n[Bridge - horns alone, then bass]\n媽媽回家笑說 簽得比我漂亮\n下次 自己簽自己的\n[Chorus]\n簽簽簽 這次簽我自己\n考卷六十分 字寫得很大\n簽簽簽 手終於不抖\n最後一撇我拉得漂亮\n[Outro - horns and bass, tight stop]",
